Not rage, pity is what I feel, for a game developer whose first commercial game looks and feels like a school project (in fact, I link a video to
's tutorial for making this very game below, thanks
). Unable to design a good platformer or even animate a simple sprite, he provides us with a blue cube in a beige 2D labyrinth made difficult by a 3D camera angle, spikes with overlarge hitboxes, and a timer. A good rage-inducing game 1. gives you something to strive for, and 2. then withholds it, laughing at our puny lack of skill. Since this game fails at step 1, it's not worth playing unless you're friends with the developer; and it's not worth paying for, either.

Just the same simulator i "played" for a while : FSX in the beginning and P3D later. The real innovation is the FPS that is really increased : even with a 3770k and a GTX980 the "game" was below 30 FPS (really high settings). Now this is really smooth and this is what  i wonder.
Another great thing is the third party devs that continues to fix problems encounter by Win10 or FSX SE (or the both).
if you are really interested in flight simulators and want to bring you more of what it is in real life you can not get away with aircraft included : there are many freeware , payware are much more realistic but cost a expensive than even the game itself ( Majestic DASH 8 or F1 ATR 72500 : about € 40 )

It's hard to get used to the keyboard controls, because yes, i don't have any controllers ;-;
It's probably one of the greatest and the most realistic flight simulators i have ever played.
( so realistic i get confused playin it )

